Let  \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
k(x) &\text{if }x>3, \\
x^2-6x+12&\text{if }x\leq3.
\end{cases}
\] Find the function $k(x)$ such that $f$ is its own inverse.

Let  \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
k(x) &\text{if }x>2, \\
2+(x-2)^2&\text{if }x\leq2.
\end{cases}
\]Find the function $k(x)$ such that $f$ is its own inverse.
